The full vocabulary in one place. When a word in the docs is unfamiliar, it is defined here.

## The five words

- **Page**: a route that ships as server HTML with no Kit client (`csr = false`). Only islands hydrate. See [How it works](/docs/start/overview).
- **Island**: a component that becomes interactive when it gets JS on a schedule. See [Client islands](/docs/regions/client-islands).
- **Lake**: static HTML *inside* an island that ships zero client JS. See [Lakes](/docs/regions/lakes).
- **Server island**: HTML fetched from the server after load. Placeholder first, no JS. See [Server islands](/docs/regions/server-islands).
- **Held region**: a server-*chosen* renderable that you place like data (`<Region of={x} />`). See [Held regions](/docs/regions/held-regions).

## Attributes & schedules

- **`wake`**: the import attribute that schedules a region: when the JS of an island runs, or when a `deferred`/`live` region fetches. `'none'` makes a lake.
- **`render`**: the delivery mode: `static` (inline HTML, the default), `deferred` (a server-island hole, fetched), `live` (a hole that revalidates).
- **`region: 'raw'`**: marks a held, server-chosen region (given to `region()` where the transform cannot see the call).
- **`keep`**: keep the node + state of a live island across SPA navigation (was `persist`).
- **`preset`**: a named bundle of attributes defined in plugin config, applied with `with { preset: 'name' }`.
- **`load` / `idle` / `visible` / `interaction` / `(media)`**: the schedules. `interaction` (islands only) wakes on the first pointer/key/focus, and replays the click that woke it. On an island, they say when JS runs. On a `deferred`/`live` region, when the HTML fetches. See [Timing & nesting](/docs/regions/timing-nesting).

## Mechanics

- **Region**: the DOM element (`<ogygia-region>`) that the runtime manages for each island, lake, or server island.
- **Runtime**: the ~7.6 KB runtime (~11.7 KB with the SPA router) that boots on a Page and wakes regions on schedule.
- **Portable binding**: a marked import whose *binding* is the island. Thus you can pass it around like a component. See [Client islands](/docs/regions/client-islands).
- **Nearest-boundary rule**: nesting is decided by the closest marked parent. See [Timing & nesting](/docs/regions/timing-nesting).
- **Dedupe**: the same component + strategy makes one client chunk, however many times it is used.

## Data & state

- **Remote function**: a Kit `query` / `command` / `form` etc., callable from inside islands. See [Remote functions](/docs/data-state/remote-functions).
- **Live region**: a held region emitted again over time by `query.live`, morphed or kept alive in place. See [Held regions](/docs/regions/held-regions).
- **Transportable**: a class that can cross an island boundary as a prop, when it declares `static wire = import.meta.og.wire({ encode, decode })`. See [Shared state](/docs/data-state/state-context#sharing-state).
- **Codec**: the `{ encode, decode }` pair on a transportable class that says how its instances travel.
- **Wire tag**: the stable identity (`module#Class`) that a transportable is registered under, on both sides.

## Content

- **Collection**: a set of content entries defined with `content()`. See [Content collections](/docs/content/collections).
- **Entry**: a single item: `{ id, data, meta, body }`, where `body` is a held region and `meta` is source-derived (for example `{ headings }`).
- **Source / loader**: where the entries of a collection come from: a `{ refs, get }` object (plus optional `init` / `live` / `groups`). `markdown()`, `json()`, `blocks()` build one from a glob. Write your own to fetch a CMS. See [Content collections](/docs/content/collections).

## PPR & single-flight

- **PPR (partial prerendering)**: a static shell baked at build, with dynamic held regions filled per visitor at request time. `export const prerender = true` + `render: 'deferred'` holes. See [Partial prerendering](/docs/app/spa-router).
- **Single-flight navigation**: on a SPA navigation, the router pulls all load holes of the incoming page down **one** batch request, not a fetch per hole. See [SPA router](/docs/app/spa-router#single-flight).
- **Parcel**: the rendered HTML of one hole in a batch response, delivered as a `<template data-ogygia-slot>`.
- **Out-of-order flush**: batched holes stream back in settle order. Thus a fast region lands before a slow one, whatever the source order.
- **Single-flight mutation**: a command that returns a region sends the re-rendered HTML back in its own response. Thus the mounted region repaints, with no follow-up fetch.
